        "My employer says only hours over 40 count. Are they wrong? Under California law, almost certainly. Daily overtime after 8 hours applies regardless of your weekly total. An employer using only the federal weekly rule in California is likely underpaying you.",
        "How far back can I claim California overtime? California generally allows up to three years for wage claims, and up to four years under the unfair-competition law. That's longer than the federal window, so don't assume you've run out of time."
